{:ev/id "vin-002" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757100120000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "vine-anatomy" {:title "Vine anatomy" :definition "The trunk carries the cordons, the cordons carry the fruiting canes, the canes carry the buds from which green shoots grow. This year's crop is born from last year's buds." :kind :definition :source-id "src-handbook" :status :accepted}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-003" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757100180000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "rootstock" {:title "Rootstock and grafting" :definition "A European variety is grafted onto American rootstock — its roots are beyond phylloxera's reach. The rootstock is chosen for the soil: lime, drought, salinity." :kind :definition :source-id "src-handbook" :status :accepted}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-004" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757100240000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "terroir" {:title "Terroir" :definition "The sum of a place: soil, relief, climate and the estate's hand. One variety on two slopes gives two different wines — that is terroir, not the winemaker's error." :kind :principle :source-id "src-handbook" :status :accepted}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-005" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757100300000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "soil" {:title "Vineyard soil" :definition "The vine likes poor, well-drained soils: on rich black earth it grows leaves instead of clusters. Stones warm up by day and give the heat back to the berries at night." :kind :definition :source-id "src-handbook" :status :accepted}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-006" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757100360000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "climate" {:title "Climate and microclimate" :definition "Macroclimate is the region, mesoclimate the slope, microclimate the air inside the canopy. The grower controls only the last one: leaves, rows, the grass between them." :kind :definition :source-id "src-handbook" :status :accepted}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-007" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757100420000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "phenology" {:title "Growth stages" :definition "Bleeding, budbreak, flowering, fruit set, berry growth, veraison, ripening, leaf fall. Every operation in the season is tied to a stage, not to a date." :kind :definition :source-id "src-handbook" :status :accepted}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-008" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757100480000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "trellis" {:title "Trellis and training" :definition "The trellis holds the canopy in a vertical plane: leaves in the sun, clusters in half-shade, airflow top to bottom. Training is the vine's skeleton the trellis carries." :kind :definition :source-id "src-handbook" :status :accepted}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-009" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757100540000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "winter-pruning" {:title "Winter pruning" :definition "Pruning decides next year's crop: too few buds means a short harvest, too many means overload and small berries. You count buds per vine, not canes." :kind :procedure :source-id "src-handbook" :status :accepted}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-010" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757100600000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "canopy" {:title "Canopy management" :definition "Removing water shoots, tying, trimming the tops, pulling leaves around the clusters. One goal: light and air for the berries, the vine's strength into fruit, not foliage." :kind :procedure :source-id "src-notes" :status :accepted}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-011" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757100660000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "veraison" {:title "Veraison" :definition "The onset of ripening: red varieties colour up, whites turn translucent, the berry softens. Growth is over — sugar starts climbing, acid falling." :kind :definition :source-id "src-handbook" :status :accepted}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-012" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757100720000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "ripeness" {:title "Ripeness: sugar and acid" :definition "Ripeness is a balance: sugar in °Bx rises while titratable acidity in g/L falls. For sparkling you pick earlier, for dessert wine later; a berry that “tastes ripe” is no argument without the numbers." :kind :principle :source-id "src-notes" :status :accepted}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-013" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757100780000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "harvest" {:title "Harvest" :definition "The date is dictated by ripeness numbers and the forecast: rain before picking dilutes the juice and splits berries. Pick in the cool of the morning — warm fruit oxidises on the way." :kind :procedure :source-id "src-notes" :status :accepted}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-014" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757100840000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "mildew" {:title "Downy and powdery mildew" :definition "Downy mildew: oily spots on top of the leaf, white down underneath, thrives in the wet. Powdery mildew: a grey dust-like coating on both sides and on berries, active even in dry weather." :kind :definition :source-id "src-handbook" :status :accepted}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-015" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757100900000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "irrigation" {:title "Irrigation" :definition "Mild water deficit before veraison is quality's ally: smaller berries, denser flavour. Irrigating before harvest waters down the future wine." :kind :procedure :source-id "src-notes" :status :accepted}]]}
