{:ev/id "vin-032" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757101920000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-vin-vine-anatomy-0" {:concept-id "vine-anatomy" :kind :diagram :level :novice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "A vine in cross-section: trunk, two cordons, a fruiting cane with eight buds and a two-bud renewal spur. Labels mark what fruits this year and what next year." :grounded-in "src-handbook" :anchor "p6" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-033" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757101980000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-vin-vine-anatomy-1" {:concept-id "vine-anatomy" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "==The green shoot from a bud carries both leaves and clusters.== Anything growing from old wood is a water shoot: almost no fruit, plenty of appetite." :grounded-in "src-handbook" :anchor "p7" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-034" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757102040000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-vin-rootstock-2" {:concept-id "rootstock" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Phylloxera ate own-rooted Europe in the 19th century; since then European varieties live on American roots. The graft is where two plants fused — the ring is visible." :grounded-in "src-handbook" :anchor "p9" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-035" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757102100000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-vin-terroir-3" {:concept-id "terroir" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "A south slope collects more heat over the season, and the upper slope escapes frost: cold air flows downhill like water. That is why mid-slope sites are the prized ones." :grounded-in "src-handbook" :anchor "p12" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-036" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757102160000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-vin-soil-4" {:concept-id "soil" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Drainage beats fertility: water standing at the roots suffocates the vine and invites disease. Gravel, limestone, slate — the three classic “poor” homes of the vine." :grounded-in "src-handbook" :anchor "p14" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-037" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757102220000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-vin-climate-5" {:concept-id "climate" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "A cluster open to morning sun and shaded at noon is managed microclimate. A dense canopy holds dew until lunch — a ready incubator for downy mildew." :grounded-in "src-handbook" :anchor "p16" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-038" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757102280000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-vin-phenology-6" {:concept-id "phenology" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Flowering is the most fragile stage: rain and cold in those ten days cut fruit set, and no later fieldwork brings it back." :grounded-in "src-handbook" :anchor "p18" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-039" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757102340000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-vin-trellis-7" {:concept-id "trellis" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Vertical shoot positioning: the bottom wire carries the fruiting cane, the paired upper wires catch the shoots. A metre of leaf wall is the vine's solar panel." :grounded-in "src-handbook" :anchor "p20" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-040" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757102400000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-vin-winter-pruning-8" {:concept-id "winter-pruning" :kind :worked-example :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "A 20-bud vine: an 8-bud fruiting cane plus a 2-bud renewal spur, the second cordon the same. The spur's shoots become next year's cane — so the vine never walks away from its trunk." :grounded-in "src-handbook" :anchor "p23" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-041" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757102460000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-vin-winter-pruning-9" {:concept-id "winter-pruning" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Prune during dormancy, after leaf fall and before bleeding. Leave the secateurs home on frosty mornings: the wood is brittle, cuts tear." :grounded-in "src-handbook" :anchor "p22" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-042" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757102520000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-vin-canopy-10" {:concept-id "canopy" :kind :worked-example :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "June: break the water shoots off the trunk, tuck shoots behind the wires, pull leaves on the east side of the clusters — morning sun dries the dew, noon sun cannot scorch." :grounded-in "src-notes" :anchor "p4" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-043" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757102580000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-vin-canopy-11" {:concept-id "canopy" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Trimming means shortening the tops once shoots outgrow the trellis: the vine stops pushing growth and switches to the fruit." :grounded-in "src-notes" :anchor "p5" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-044" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757102640000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-vin-veraison-12" {:concept-id "veraison" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Veraison starts the countdown to harvest: 30–40 days for early varieties, up to 70 for late ones. From that day the berry also baits wasps and birds — time for the nets." :grounded-in "src-handbook" :anchor "p27" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-045" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757102700000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-vin-ripeness-13" {:concept-id "ripeness" :kind :worked-example :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "A 100-berry sample from different vines and both row sides: ++22 °Bx at 6 g/L acid — time to plan picking for a dry red++; 18 °Bx at 9 g/L — keep waiting, though for sparkling it is ready now." :grounded-in "src-notes" :anchor "p8" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-046" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757102760000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-vin-ripeness-14" {:concept-id "ripeness" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Beyond the numbers there is physiology: ++brown seeds, a berry that detaches easily, flesh with no green taste++. ==The numbers decide, physiology confirms.==" :grounded-in "src-notes" :anchor "p9" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-047" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757102820000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-vin-harvest-15" {:concept-id "harvest" :kind :worked-example :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "The forecast promises rain in two days, sugar is on target, acid a touch high: pick now — a little extra freshness beats rain-diluted juice and grey rot afterwards." :grounded-in "src-notes" :anchor "p11" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-048" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757102880000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-vin-harvest-16" {:concept-id "harvest" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Shallow crates of 15–20 kg: under its own weight the fruit crushes and the juice oxidises before the press. Rotten clusters are culled in the row, not at the sorting table." :grounded-in "src-notes" :anchor "p12" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-049" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757102940000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-vin-mildew-17" {:concept-id "mildew" :kind :diagram :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "A leaf in two panes: left, downy mildew — an oily spot on top, white down strictly underneath; right, powdery — grey “dust” on both sides. Caption: down below means downy, dust everywhere means powdery." :grounded-in "src-handbook" :anchor "p30" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-050" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757103000000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-vin-mildew-18" {:concept-id "mildew" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Prevention beats cure: an airy canopy, spraying before the rain rather than after. Once you see the spots, assume a week is already lost." :grounded-in "src-handbook" :anchor "p31" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "vin-051" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757103060000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-vin-irrigation-19" {:concept-id "irrigation" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Drip at the root at dawn: less evaporation, not a drop on the leaves. Thirst shows as drooping tendrils and stalled shoot tips — not as “the ground looks dry”." :grounded-in "src-notes" :anchor "p14" :is :object}]]}
